Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 00:17:39 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Resolve relative IRIs against a base IRI (base_iri,
 rml:baseIRI)

An IRI term map that generates a relative IRI wrote it as it is ("<Carlos>"),
which is not valid N-Triples. RML-Core resolves it against the base IRI: the
rml:baseIRI of the triples map, else the base IRI given to the processor.
The RML-Core test cases RMLTC0019a, 0020a and 0026a-d (kg-construct/rml-core)
expect it.

The new option base_iri of the CONFIGURATION section gives the base IRI
(none by default: the output is unchanged), and the rml:baseIRI of a triples
map takes its place for that triples map. Tests: test/base-iri.
